.SH "v3\&.0\&.0 - 2023-12-18"
.PP
.SS "Changed"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: date-fns is now a dual-package with the support of both ESM and CommonJS\&. The files exports are now explicitly in the \fRpackage\&.json\fP\&. The ESM files now have \fR\&.mjs\fP extension\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: The package now has a flat structure, meaning functions are now named \fRnode_modules/date-fns/add\&.mjs\fP, locales are \fRnode_modules/date-fns/locale/enUS\&.mjs\fP, etc\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: Now all file content’s exported via named exports instead of \fRexport default\fP, which will require change direct imports i\&.e\&. \fRconst addDays = require(‘date-fns/addDays’)\fP to \fRconst { addDays } = require(‘date-fns/addDays’)\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: TypeScript types are now completely rewritten, check out the \fRd\&.ts\fP files for more information\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: \fRconstants\fP now is not exported via the index, so to import one use \fRimport { daysInYear } from "date-fns/constants";\fP\&. It improves compatibility with setups that modularize imports \fRlike Next\&.js\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: Functions now don’t check the number of passed arguments, delegating this task to type checkers\&. The functions are now slimmer because of this\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP The arguments are not explicitly converted to the target types\&. Instead, they are passed as is, delegating this task to type checkers\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: Functions that accept \fRInterval\fP arguments now do not throw an error if the start is before the end and handle it as a negative interval\&. If one of the properties in an \fRInvalid Date\fP, these functions also do not throw and handle them as invalid intervals\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRareIntervalsOverlapping\fP normalize intervals before comparison, so \fR{ start: a, end: b }\fP is practically equivalent to \fR{ start: b, end: a }\fP\&. When comparing intervals with one of the properties being \fRInvalid Date\fP, the function will return false unless the others are valid and equal, given the \fRinclusive\fP option is passed\&. Otherwise, and when even one of the intervals has both properties invalid, the function will always return \fRfalse\fP\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRgetOverlappingDaysInIntervals\fP now normalizes intervals before comparison, so \fR{ start: a, end: b }\fP is practically equivalent to \fR{ start: b, end: a }\fP\&. If any of the intervals’ properties is an \fRInvalid Date\fP, the function will always return 0\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRisWithinInterval\fP now normalizes intervals before comparison, so \fR{ start: a, end: b }\fP is practically equivalent to \fR{ start: b, end: a }\fP\&. If any of the intervals’ properties is an \fRInvalid Date\fP, the function will always return false\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRintervalToDuration\fP now returns negative durations for negative intervals\&. If one or both of the interval properties are invalid, the function will return an empty object\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The eachXOfInterval functions (\fReachDayOfInterval\fP, \fReachHourOfInterval\fP, \fReachMinuteOfInterval\fP, \fReachMonthOfInterval\fP, \fReachWeekendOfInterval\fP, \fReachWeekendOfMonth\fP, \fReachWeekendOfYear\fP, \fReachWeekOfInterval\fP, \fReachYearOfInterval\fP) now return a reversed array if the passed interval’s start is after the end\&. Invalid properties will result in an empty array\&. Functions that accept the \fRstep\fP option now also allow negative, 0, and NaN values and return reversed results if the step is negative and an empty array otherwise\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: \fRintervalToDuration\fP now skips 0 values in the resulting duration, resulting in more compact objects with only relevant properties\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: \fRroundToNearestMinutes\fP now returns \fRInvalid Date\fP instead of throwing an error when \fRnearestTo\fP option is less than 1 or more than 30\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: IE is no longer supported\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: Now all functions use \fRMath\&.trunc\fP rounding method where rounding is required\&. The behavior is configurable on a per-function basis\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: Undocumented \fRonlyNumeric\fP option was removed from \fRnn\fP and \fRsv\fP locales\&. If you relied on it, \fRplease contact me\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: Flow is not supported anymore\&. If you relied on it, \fRplease contact me\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: The locales now use regular functions instead of the UTC version, which should not break any code unless you used locales directly\&.
.PP
.SS "Added"
.IP "\(bu" 2
All functions that accept date arguments now also accept strings\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
All functions now export options interfaces\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Now functions allow passing custom Date extensions like \fRUTCDate\fP\&. They will detect and use the arguments constructor to generate the result of the same class\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fReachMonthOfInterval\fP, \fReachQuarterOfInterval\fP, \fReachWeekOfInterval\fP, and \fReachYearOfInterval\fP now accept the \fRstep\fP option like most of the eachXOfInterval functions\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A new \fRinterval\fP function that validates interval, emulating the v2 interval functions behavior\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdifferenceInX\fP functions now accept options and allow setting up \fRroundingMethod\fP that configures how the result is rounded\&. \fRMath\&.trunc\fP is the default method\&.
.PP
