.IP "\(bu" 2
Fixed bug in Galician locale caused by incorrect usage of \fRgetHours\fP instead of \fRgetUTCHours\fP\&.
.PP
.SS "Changed"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBREAKING\fP: now functions don't accept string arguments, but only numbers or dates\&. When a string is passed, it will result in an unexpected result (\fRInvalid Date\fP, \fRNaN\fP, etc)\&.

.PP
From now on a string should be parsed using \fRparseISO\fP (ISO 8601) or \fRparse\fP\&.

.PP
In v1 we've used \fRnew Date()\fP to parse strings, but it resulted in many hard-to-track bugs caused by inconsistencies in different browsers\&. To address that we've implemented our ISO 8601 parser but that made library to significantly grow in size\&. To prevent inevitable bugs and keep the library tiny, we made this trade-off\&.

.PP
See \fRthis post\fP for more details\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Before v2\&.0\&.0
addDays("2016\-01\-01", 1);

// v2\&.0\&.0 onward
addDays(parseISO("2016\-01\-01"), 1);
.fi
.PP

